// expect: refuse E_HandlerInexhaustive
// A handler is exhaustive over every effect its arms answer — the
// match-exhaustiveness law at a handler. `only_inc` answers `inc` alone, and
// its install subtracts the whole of `State` from the body's row by name, so
// `f`'s declared `!State` was a FALSE ABSENCE PROOF: on boot 16286d94 this
// program compiled clean and `get()`, walking past the install at runtime,
// read garbage evidence at the root (exit 134). The declaration refuses now,
// naming the op no arm answers; forwarding it (`get() => resume(get())`)
// or declaring `inc` as its own effect is the honest form
// (tests/micros/mn-handler-forwarding-arm.mn).
effect State {
  inc() -> Int
  get() -> Int
}

handler only_inc {
  inc() => resume(1),
}

fn f() with !State = get() + inc() ~> only_inc

fn main() -> Int = f()
